This add-on assumes the MKL library to be available and installed.

INSTALLATION & USAGE::
====================

- Use a recent version of MKL (version must be at least 10.0).

- Build tfem using:

    make all mkl_gmres

  for a usual build + mkl_gmres.

- Edit Mdefs.mk for use with the MKL library.

Remarks:

 - use an iterative solver only when the direct solver needs too much memory.
 
 - for a velocity-pressure to work you need to renumber the unknowns such that
   the pressures are at the end of the system vector (see userguide).

 - renumbering for minimal fill-in in sparse matrix LU-decomposition seems to
   be affect memory use and/or convergence rate. Use the add-on metis for that
   or use renumbering already in your external meshgenerator.

 - experiment with the parameters, for example droptol>0 may decrease the
   computation time.

 - when you need large fillins you might better use a direct solver, such as
   ma41, which is usually much faster.

 - for the ILUT preconditioner, it is recommended to set zero_diag_par=0 
   (this is the default) otherwise a careful choice of zero_diag_comp must be
   done to avoid that the program aborts.

 - for ILU0 preconditioner, zero_diag_par should be set to 1. Indeed, in this
   case, a zero value on the diagonal (for the solver, "zero value" means that
   it is less than zero_diag_comp) is substituted with the value in
   zero_diag_value. If zero_diag_par = 0, the ILU0 cannot be built and
   the program aborts, at least for a Stokes problem.

-  notice that the parameter "maxfil" is an integer parameter used for the
   fill-in if larger than zero (default is maxfil=0). The default is to 
   use the "fillin" parameter similar to the sparskit fillin parameter, which
   scales with the matrix size, whereas maxfil does not.
